  "body": "The README introduction still implies no tracking, despite the detailed privacy section describing browser storage and service requests. This corrects that sentence and adds an R001B whole-document guard against contradictory privacy claims. The previously delivered Windows and clock documentation is preserved.\r\n\r\nValidation: exact-source independent review passed; the integrated R001B run has 4 PASS and 8 guarded reuse dispositions, with four discriminating refusal controls retained. Frozen V1 verification and diff checks pass. Runtime, generated entries, configuration, installers and V1 are unchanged.\r\n\r\nAdvances #27. Public desktop/narrow table and builder-link evidence, final qualification, delivery readbacks and the whole-issue closure certificate remain required. This PR does not close the issue automatically. The test-script change requires the owner's exact-head merge/deployment approval.\r\n",
